{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454680-the-song-of-the-aegean-a-supplement-for-vampire-the-dark-ages","id":1454680,"title":"The Song of the Aegean - A Supplement for Vampire: the Dark Ages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-11T04:35:48-07:00","id":1454680,"title":"The Song of the Aegean - A Supplement for Vampire: the Dark Ages","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><img src=\"https://dtrpg-public-files.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1/363873-thumb140.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Ancient Lands and New Rulers</b><br /> <br /> The bloody conquests of the Fourth Crusade unleashed a wave of chaos across the Eastern Mediterranean. In the Aegean, ambitious lords from Western Europe have carved out a number of petty states, seeking to enrich themselves at the expense of their former allies in the Byzantine Empire. Such conquests have unleashed tensions across the region, as the politics, culture, and religion of the new rulers of the region come into conflict with their subjects. These struggles are not confined to the mortal populations of the Aegean, with the Cainites of the Eastern Mediterranean competing over dominance of the region. The tides of history have shifted, and the consequences will play out for many centuries to come.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <b>The Aegean by Night</b><br /> <br /> <i>The Song of the Aegean</i> is a location sourcebook for <i>Vampire: the Dark Ages</i>, focused on the Latin states of Southern Greece. The book provides a detailed exploration of the key domain of Athens, as well as information on the history, geography, and current military and political struggles affecting the region. This includes:</span></span></span><ul><li>Information on a number of key locations in the Aegean</li> <li>Profiles of 11 characters, ranging from the Cainite population of Athens, to the Oracle of Trophonius.</li> <li>Maps, timelines, and other reference material to support chronicles based in the Aegean</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>The Song of the Aegean</i> is a Year of the Tide product for <i>Vampire: the Dark Ages</i>.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T19:54:44-07:00","id":1454713,"title":"","content":"Love your work, James. Is there enough earlier history in the book that it would be complementary with Vampire: The Classic Age?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T04:32:28-07:00","id":1454729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454680-the-song-of-the-aegean-a-supplement-for-vampire-the-dark-ages?p=1454713#post1454713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Love your work, James. Is there enough earlier history in the book that it would be complementary with Vampire: The Classic Age?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>The Song of the Aegean</i> specifically focuses on the medieval history of Greece; in practical terms, managing the contents of a book like this means that you may be choosing to exclude material that is relatively remote from the period which is focused upon. Thus, for instance, the history of Athens in <i>The Song of the Aegean</i> only begins in 267 AD; that gives a thousand years of history, looking, in particular at the transformation of the Aegean from a Roman province to the patchwork of petty states present in the thirteenth century. The only Cainite in Athens who existed for long enough to remember the ancient world is the prince, Dionysius; this does, of course, give him some very different perspectives to many of the other Cainites in the region.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T05:39:29-07:00","id":1454736,"title":"","content":"Really good supplements. Well documented and detailed. In the Storytellers Vault, England Will Burn, The Gates of Damascus that I liked the most, and I think I will appreciarte The Aegean Song too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T11:16:11-07:00","id":1454754,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.kenandrobintalkaboutstuff.com/index.php/episode-451-bring-a-bunch-of-idiots/\" target=\"_blank\">A discussion of the Frankokratia, or when the Franks ruled Greece, was discussed on a recent episode of Ken and Robin Talk About Stuff.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T13:02:57-07:00","id":1454765,"title":"","content":"Do you have a link handy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T16:55:10-07:00","id":1454774,"title":"","content":"My comment is the link itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T20:34:05-07:00","id":1454784,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I mea\u200bnt <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar317_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"317\" data-vbnamecard=\"317\">James_Willoughby</a>. A link to<i> Song of the Aegea\u200bn</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T21:11:18-07:00","id":1454789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454680-the-song-of-the-aegean-a-supplement-for-vampire-the-dark-ages?p=1454729#post1454729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>The Song of the Aegean</i> specifically focuses on the medieval history of Greece; in practical terms, managing the contents of a book like this means that you may be choosing to exclude material that is relatively remote from the period which is focused upon. Thus, for instance, the history of Athens in <i>The Song of the Aegean</i> only begins in 267 AD; that gives a thousand years of history, looking, in particular at the transformation of the Aegean from a Roman province to the patchwork of petty states present in the thirteenth century. The only Cainite in Athens who existed for long enough to remember the ancient world is the prince, Dionysius; this does, of course, give him some very different perspectives to many of the other Cainites in the region.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Awesome. Thanks. I'll pick it up come payday. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T21:41:25-07:00","id":1454793,"title":"","content":"Here's a <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?discount=916e1b7165\" target=\"_blank\">product link</a>, with a small discount for forum users; the discount will last to the end of the month. I will be adding further material at some point, at which point the price will go up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T09:58:54-07:00","id":1454840,"title":"","content":"Just purchased it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Really like the quality <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's great resources to flesh out my game. (I recently perchased the France by Night book... very beautiful too).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8757-pram","name":"Pram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-14T03:20:49-07:00","id":1454872,"title":"","content":"As a bit of context, <i>The Song of the Aegean</i> was written as a break from other projects, to fit in with the <i>Year of the Tide</i>. The intention, over the longer term, is to include one full chapter for each of the Latin states in the Aegean (bar the Marquisate of Bodonitsa, which is a castle and a bunch of wilderness), plus a number of interesting smaller locations in the final chapter. <br /> <br /> The Frankokratia provides a particularly interesting situation in which to set chronicles, as it presents a society in flux, and many of the forces affecting the region in this time have obvious dramatic applications within a game. It's also pretty easy to tie into published supplements, as you can easily start off a chronicle with <i>Constantinople by Night</i> and <i>Bitter Crusade</i>, and then move on to <i>The Song of the Aegean</i> after the Fourth Crusade.<br /> <br /> Anyway, here's a discount code for <i><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?discount=9b3d66331a\" target=\"_blank\">The Gates of Damascus</a></i> for anyone who doesn't already have it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-14T07:42:05-07:00","id":1454885,"title":"","content":"What is <i>Year of the Tide</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-14T15:24:15-07:00","id":1454912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454680-the-song-of-the-aegean-a-supplement-for-vampire-the-dark-ages?p=1454885#post1454885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is <i>Year of the Tide</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Each year Storytellers Vault Writers/Artists do a theme run- last year was Year of the Road......or was that the year before? Basically its just a thing to help spark ideas and give a thrust to that years releases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-14T17:33:17-07:00","id":1454922,"title":"","content":"So the year has a vaguely nautical theme?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-14T19:59:07-07:00","id":1454934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454680-the-song-of-the-aegean-a-supplement-for-vampire-the-dark-ages?p=1454922#post1454922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the year has a vaguely nautical theme?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the word Tide is being very broadly interpreted by various authors but mostly, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}